    {
      "text": "When the stars flicker in the night sky, it flutters about, scattering a glowing powder.",
      "version": "x"
    },
    {
      "text": "The spot patterns on its back grow larger or smaller depending on the number of stars in the night sky.",
      "version": "y"
    },
    {
      "text": "It is said that in lands with clean air, where the stars fill the sky, there live Ledian in countless numbers. There is a good reason for this—the Pokémon uses the light of the stars as its energy.",
      "version": "omega-ruby"
    },
    {
      "text": "It is said that in lands with clean air, where the stars fill the sky, there live Ledian in countless numbers. There is a good reason for this—the Pokémon uses the light of the stars as its energy.",
      "version": "alpha-sapphire"
    },
    {
      "text": "While it’s believed that starlight provides it with energy, this Pokémon also loves to eat berries. In the daytime, it curls up in the grass to sleep.",
      "version": "sun"
    },
    {
      "text": "In battle, it throws punches with all four arms. The power of each individual blow is piddly, so it aims to win by quantity rather than quality.",
      "version": "moon"
    },
    {
      "text": "It’s said that the patterns on its back are related to the stars in the night sky, but the details of that relationship remain unclear.",
      "version": "ultra-sun"
    },
    {
      "text": "It flies through the night sky, sprinkling sparkly dust. According to some, if that dust sticks to you, good things will happen to you.",
      "version": "ultra-moon"
    }
  ],
